{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, upon Shoshan Edut</b> — the meaning is that it is the beginning tune of a piyyut: Shoshan Edut. Some say that Shoshan is the name of an instrument, and they interpret עדות like עדי, and like it: את הנזר ואת העדות." "And the meaning of ללמד — that he commanded that the singers teach it to him, to always recall HaShem's kindness, whose hand prevailed in battle after he had grown weak."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:19.822280011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}